[{"annotations":["164|7|disease|MESH:D005221","121|9|disease|None","113|7|disease|MESH:D005221"],"text":" On the other hand large artery elasticity but not small artery elasticity was related to both reduced perceived fatigue/tiredness while at rest as well as central fatigue during maximal isometric contractions suggesting that brain function may be influenced by arterial elasticity.","pmcid":"PMC3910517","score":0.7813067346811294,"pmid":24511534,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["346|23|disease|MESH:D014652"],"text":"Analysis of the diastolic radial pulse waveform provides an assessment of artery elasticity at the level of the aorta and conduit arteries [large artery elasticity (LAE)] and the peripheral branches and microvascular components [small artery elasticity (SAE)] that contains information about structural and functional vascular changes, including endothelial dysfunction.","pmcid":"PMC2764552","score":0.7246871554851532,"pmid":19731451,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["0|16|disease|MESH:D001161","50|10|disease|None"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis, characterized by remodeling and stiffening of large elastic arteries is the most significant manifestation of vascular aging.","pmcid":null,"score":0.7224286895990372,"pmid":15820199,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["107|23|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Non invasive assessment of large arteries structure and function is a valuable tool for early detection of athero/arteriosclerosis and the cardiovascular risk.","pmcid":null,"score":0.7219304078817368,"pmid":17802929,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["52|26|disease|MESH:D014652","0|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis is the general term for a group of arterial vascular diseases characterized by arterial wall thickening and loss of elasticity, which are caused by different biological processes.","pmcid":null,"score":0.7197884839773178,"pmid":31435781,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["186|3|disease|MESH:D002318","37|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arterial stiffness reflects systemic arteriosclerosis at various sites in the vascular tree, most notably in large elastic arteries, and is believed to play a role in the development of CVD.","pmcid":"PMC8492401","score":0.714493522644043,"pmid":34703940,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":null,"text":"In a study of African-American youth (mean age = 12 years old), showed that vigilance was inversely related to large arterial elasticity (a preclinical index of cardiovascular function) for boys but not girls.","pmcid":"PMC5555118","score":0.7130780202150345,"pmid":25581238,"section":"COMP_INT"},{"annotations":["208|16|disease|MESH:D001161","181|14|disease|MESH:D058186"],"text":"Abnormal left ventricular geometry is the most common target-organ damage, and other damages include increased vascular intima-media thickness, reduced arterial elasticity, reduced renal function, and fundus arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC6500570","score":0.7118531286716461,"pmid":31080465,"section":"METHODS"},{"annotations":["0|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis is a disease effecting large elastic, elastic muscular and large muscular arteries.","pmcid":null,"score":0.7113153874874115,"pmid":19419126,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":null,"text":"Biologically, in this age group, large artery elasticity functions well and only peripheral vascular resistance can increase diastolic blood pressure.","pmcid":"PMC4690591","score":0.7111473786830902,"pmid":26694755,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["61|6|disease|None"],"text":"Large arterial elasticity varies as a function of gender and racism-related vigilance in black youth.","pmcid":null,"score":0.7110592776536941,"pmid":16982392,"section":"title"},{"annotations":["340|3|gene|5741","97|19|disease|MESH:D006961","8|48|disease|MESH:D061205"],"text":"Valvular, myocardial and vascular ectopic calcifications may be considered structural effects of hyperparathyroidism, whereas elevated aortic pulse pressure and lessened large artery elasticity, impaired endothelial functions, and local regulation of vascular tone (vasoconstriction or vasodilation) may be considered functional effects of PTH on the cardiovascular system.","pmcid":"PMC5324883","score":0.7097144538164138,"pmid":27147401,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["215|13|disease|None","524|7|species|9606","230|16|disease|MESH:D001161","283|11|disease|MESH:D006984"],"text":"Extensive vascular studies with high resolution ultrasound, oscillometry and tonometry will be performed at the carotid bed, the femoral bed, the aorta, the upper arm and lower limbs and retina in order to evaluate atheromatosis, arteriosclerosis/elasticity, arterial remodeling and hypertrophy endothelial function, wave reflections and aortic hemodynamics, retinal geometry (Table 2) in 2 to 5 sequential visits within 6-9 months (visit 0, visit 1=1 week, visit 2= 1 month, visit 3= 3 months, visit 4 >= 6 months) in each patient starting from disease onset/relapse to complete remission.","pmcid":"PMC7046042","score":0.709432492852211,"pmid":32185320,"section":"METHODS"},{"annotations":["262|13|disease|MESH:D006333","229|28|disease|MESH:D017379","174|28|disease|MESH:D002318","211|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"A decrease in the vascular compliance of the large elastic vessels (reduction of their \"Windkessel\" function) is of decisive importance for the pathogenesis and prognosis of cardiovascular complications such as arteriosclerosis, left ventricular hypertrophy and heart failure.","pmcid":null,"score":0.708563819527626,"pmid":7600926,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["112|12|disease|MESH:D006973","9|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"However, arteriosclerosis, which concerns the whole arterial system, contributes, in combination with aging and hypertension, to an increase in pulse pressure and wave reflection since arterial wall stiffening hampers the buffering (\"windkessel\") function of large arteries.","pmcid":"PMC9917724","score":0.7078947979211807,"pmid":36769746,"section":null},{"annotations":null,"text":"Two detected a significant improvement of endothelial function and one indicated a decrease in large artery elasticity (Table 1).","pmcid":"PMC8005536","score":0.7078668749332429,"pmid":33791343,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["46|3|disease|MESH:D002318","152|9|disease|MESH:C566112","0|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis is the pathological basis of CVD, which is caused by changes in the structure and function of the media, primarily leading to arterial stiffness, especially in the large arteries.","pmcid":"PMC8563701","score":0.7076393473148346,"pmid":34746254,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["99|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"CF-PWV reflected the elastic state of large arteries and was mainly used to evaluate the degree of arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC12329251","score":0.7068142300844192,"pmid":40777585,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":null,"text":"CONCLUSION: Conventional HD resulting in substantial plasma volume removal do not alter large artery elastic properties, whereas intrinsic microvascular venular dilator function is markedly impaired, an effect directly associated with the increase in hemoconcentration.","pmcid":null,"score":0.7063160425424576,"pmid":31734376,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["351|8|gene|None","406|8|gene|None","183|7|gene|2006","234|7|chemical|MESH:D002118","214|8|gene|None","297|31|disease|MESH:D003643","0|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis describes loss of the elasticity of the arterial wall due to an increased volume of extracellular matrix, hypertrophy of vascular smooth muscle cells, degradation of elastin, deposition of stiffer collagen fibres and calcium, and, under certain conditions, extensive formation of advanced glycation end-products, which cross-link the collagen molecules resulting in a functionally stiffer collagen matrix.","pmcid":"PMC6696433","score":0.7061563211679459,"pmid":31366035,"section":"METHODS"},{"annotations":["136|16|disease|MESH:D001161","154|19|disease|MESH:D006965","109|18|disease|MESH:D006984"],"text":"The posterior muscle consistently had higher incidences of intramural coronary arteries affected by vascular medial hypertrophy, medial arteriosclerosis, intimal hyperplasia, and/or disruption or loss of the internal elastic lamina.","pmcid":null,"score":0.705140027999878,"pmid":33094690,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["36|3|gene|1401"],"text":"However, there was no difference in CRP, HOMA-IR, or measures of cardiovascular function including pulse rate, pulse pressure, mean arterial pressure, cardiac output, systemic vascular resistance, small and large artery elasticity index.","pmcid":null,"score":0.7050855004787445,"pmid":26489823,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["38|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"The ambulatory blood pressure-related arteriosclerosis index is a series of indicators derived from ABPM that reflect the elastic function of arteries; the application scope of AB-PM in clinical has been further expanded.","pmcid":"PMC9167089","score":0.7048179012537003,"pmid":35686157,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["224|7|chemical|MESH:D002118","0|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis, characterized by the thickening and hardening of arterial walls, largely results from structural and functional shifts, such as the replacement of elastic fibers with collagen, damage to muscle fibers, and calcium deposits.","pmcid":"PMC12912415","score":0.703930345773697,"pmid":41776052,"section":null},{"annotations":["247|6|disease|MESH:D020521","262|6|disease|MESH:D020521","184|18|disease|MESH:C566112"],"text":"Along with Large Artery Elasticity index (LAE) and Small Artery Elasticity (SAE) index measures, systemic vascular resistance (SVR) and total vascular impedance (TVI) were measured as arterial stiffness parameters with measurements of pulse rate, stroke volume, stroke volume index, cardiac output, cardiac index, and cardiac ejection time to ascertain cardiac functioning.","pmcid":"PMC9115939","score":0.7029213511943817,"pmid":35581554,"section":"METHODS"},{"annotations":["172|16|disease|MESH:D001161","24|2|chemical|MESH:C038809"],"text":"Continuous elevation of BP will lead to structural and functional changes in the arterial walls, resulting in further decrease of large arterial elasticity, which reflects arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC5658088","score":0.7011325377225875,"pmid":29073198,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["0|16|disease|MESH:D001161","188|7|gene|2006","246|7|gene|2006"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis is a degenerative process that affects the extracellular matrix in the media of large elastic arteries; it is marked by thinning, splitting, fraying, and fragmentation of elastin fibers, as well as loss of orderly arrangement of elastin fibers and elastic laminae fragmentation, accompanied by collagenous remodeling.","pmcid":"PMC8516717","score":0.6997334218025207,"pmid":34601961,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["139|16|disease|MESH:D001161","331|15|disease|MESH:D050197","52|16|disease|None","96|11|disease|MESH:D000419","462|6|chemical|MESH:D008055","278|7|gene|2006"],"text":"Based on these findings it could be speculated that microalbuminuria and a high normal range of albuminuria of > 1.5 mg/mmol reflects both arteriosclerosis (vascular function), i.e. morphological characteristics of the tunica media of large elastic arteries involving decreased elastin and higher collagen content, and subclinical atherosclerosis (vascular structure), which is associated with narrowing of the arterial lumen secondary to accumulating cells and lipids in the tunica intima.","pmcid":"PMC7409481","score":0.6989400416612626,"pmid":32758145,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":null,"text":"The system determined capacitive compliance of the proximal aorta and major branches [large-artery elasticity index (LAEI)], sinusoidal oscillatory compliance of the distal arteries [small-artery elasticity index (SAEI)], and systemic vascular resistance (SVR), all indirect measures of endothelial function.","pmcid":"PMC2599761","score":0.6981209045648575,"pmid":19079718,"section":"METHODS"},{"annotations":["299|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Moreover, the nonenzymatic modifications of collagens and lipoproteins by AGEs in large vessels will result in increased collagen deposition, altering the structural integrity of arteries, disarray of elastic fibers, and the degeneration of smooth muscle tissue, which are key pathogenic factors in arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC9030615","score":0.6975607496500016,"pmid":35454131,"section":null},{"annotations":["70|14|disease|MESH:D016893","56|8|species|9606"],"text":"CONCLUSION: The large artery elasticity function in the patients with carotid plaque was poor.","pmcid":null,"score":0.6970449984073639,"pmid":29263476,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["57|16|disease|MESH:D001161","78|15|disease|MESH:D050197","121|4|disease|MESH:D056784"],"text":"Small and large artery elasticity indices are markers of arteriosclerosis and atherosclerosis respectively and linked to WMLs.","pmcid":"PMC4540324","score":0.6952883929014206,"pmid":25690663,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["184|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Influenced by various factors, such as age and high blood pressure, an intense restructuring process takes place in the viscoelastic properties of the large vessel walls, resulting in arteriosclerosis characterised by the formation of hardened arteries, i.e., reduced arterial elasticity or compliance.","pmcid":"PMC5857025","score":0.694885510802269,"pmid":29643875,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["605|26|disease|MESH:D050197","223|16|disease|MESH:D001161","134|26|disease|MESH:D050197","267|12|disease|MESH:D006973","354|16|disease|MESH:D001161","281|8|disease|MESH:D003920","372|32|disease|MESH:D001157","542|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Understanding the relationship between CF-PWV and ABI, on the one hand, we could understand the occurrence and progress of lower limb atherosclerosis obliterans; on the other hand, we could pay attention to the progress of arteriosclerosis degree in advance, such as hypertension, diabetes and other risk factors can lead to the increase of large artery arteriosclerosis, occlusion of lower limb arteries, etc., which can detect the abnormal elasticity of large arteries in advance, give early intervention in time, reduce the progression of arteriosclerosis, and then reduce the occurrence of lower limb atherosclerosis obliterans.","pmcid":"PMC12329251","score":0.6947048825025559,"pmid":40777585,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["50|10|disease|MESH:D002318","200|7|chemical|MESH:D002118"],"text":"Markers of CV health that associate with clinical CV disease include carotid artery intima-media thickness (IMT), large artery elasticity, endothelial function, left ventricular geometry, presence of calcium in the coronary arteries, and retinal vascular architecture.","pmcid":"PMC4857790","score":0.6946248334646226,"pmid":27168729,"section":null},{"annotations":["243|8|disease|MESH:D003291"],"text":"In this large multi-ethnic cohort, we found that higher large arterial stiffness measured by pulse pressure and decreased small (SAE) and large arterial elasticity (LAE) were significantly and linearly associated with faster decline in kidney function among persons with eGFR >60 ml/min/1.73m2.","pmcid":"PMC3242889","score":0.694555379152298,"pmid":22000727,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["183|15|disease|MESH:D050197","203|16|disease|MESH:D001161","0|2|disease|MESH:D057772"],"text":"VA includes a large spectrum of alterations affecting the functional and structural components of the arterial wall irrespective of size, traditionally included in the definitions of atherosclerosis and arteriosclerosis (Figure 1).","pmcid":"PMC7614971","score":0.6941985017061234,"pmid":36738307,"section":null},{"annotations":["195|3|disease|MESH:D002318"],"text":"Continuous elevated of TyG index will lead to structural and functional changes in the arterial walls, resulting in further decrease of large arterial elasticity, and these changes could lead to CVD onset.","pmcid":"PMC8830002","score":0.6937765491008758,"pmid":35144621,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["115|15|disease|MESH:D050197","21|13|disease|None","0|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis and atheromatosis are etiologically and pathogenetically different non-physiological processes in atherosclerosis localized in the proximal segments of the arterial bed and elastic-type arteries; both affect the structure and function of the arterial wall.","pmcid":null,"score":0.693559804558754,"pmid":23789446,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":null,"text":"C1 (large artery elasticity) and C2 (small artery elasticity) are functional markers for large and small arteries, respectively, derived from the third-order Windkessel model, with higher values indicating greater elasticity (and lower stiffness).","pmcid":"PMC12533632","score":0.6923846375942231,"pmid":40654243,"section":null},{"annotations":["89|8|chemical|MESH:D006854"],"text":"Other variables that were measured in some of the clinical trials in this review include cortisol; flow-mediated dilation of the brachial artery, which is a marker of endothelial function, small and large artery elasticity, and quality of life.","pmcid":"PMC7760201","score":0.6923622238636017,"pmid":33266002,"section":"RESULTS"},{"annotations":["111|16|disease|MESH:D001161","269|12|disease|MESH:D058226","203|15|disease|MESH:D050197","0|18|disease|MESH:D050379"],"text":"Arteriolosclerosis is due to stiffening, with loss of elasticity, of arterioles and must be distinguished from arteriosclerosis, a hardening with loss of elasticity of medium or large arteries, and from atherosclerosis, a stiffening of an artery specifically due to an atheromatous plaque.","pmcid":"PMC4169693","score":0.6910215437412263,"pmid":25243060,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["673|16|disease|MESH:D001161","525|23|disease|MESH:D014652","580|18|disease|MESH:D014652","82|6|disease|MESH:D020521"],"text":"The pulse pressure mainly depends on the ejection rate of the left ventricle, the stroke volume of the heart, and factors such as the compliance of the large arteries and the pressure reflection waves of the peripheral blood vessels, and as the pulse pressure increases, its damage to blood vessels is also strengthened; the tube wall is in a state of high tension for a long time; it is easy to fatigue and break, and the factor that regulates the vasoconstriction and relaxation function is out of proportion, and vascular endothelial dysfunction strengthens the progression of vascular sclerosis; therefore, pulse pressure has a certain role in reflecting the degree of arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC9167089","score":0.6904579043388367,"pmid":35686157,"section":"METHODS"},{"annotations":["41|16|disease|MESH:D001161","62|22|disease|MESH:D050380","0|28|disease|MESH:D061205"],"text":"Vascular media calcification, also named arteriosclerosis, or Monckebergs' sclerosis, is characterized by concentric calcifications in the tunica media of large elastic arteries, medium-sized visceral and renal arteries, as well as in small transitional arteries.","pmcid":"PMC7246472","score":0.6900346332788467,"pmid":32366042,"section":null},{"annotations":["106|3|disease|MESH:D003327","114|32|disease|MESH:D002539","171|14|disease|MESH:D016893","157|8|species|9606","148|4|disease|MESH:D002539","82|22|disease|MESH:D003327"],"text":"OBJECTIVE: To evaluate the relationship between large artery elastic function and coronary heart disease (CHD) or lower extremity arterial disease (LEAD) in patients with carotid plaque.","pmcid":null,"score":0.6893302017450332,"pmid":29263476,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["49|3|disease|MESH:D003924","66|3|disease|MESH:D003924","32|15|disease|MESH:D003924"],"text":"Regression analyses compared 41 type 2 diabetes (T2D) and 131 non-T2D cognitively normal elderly males on the associations of arterial wall function measures [large artery elasticity index (LAEI), small artery elasticity index (SAEI), systemic vascular resistance (SVR), and total vascular impedance (TVI)] with cognitive performance (memory, language, and executive functions), controlling for socio-demographic and cardiovascular factors.","pmcid":"PMC5754925","score":0.6891447705030441,"pmid":25352451,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["89|5|gene|8542"],"text":"Methods and Results Using linear regression, we examined cross-sectional associations of APOL1 risk genotypes (high=2 risk alleles, low=0 or 1 risk allele) with subclinical measures of vascular function (small arterial elasticity, n=1586; large arterial elasticity, n=1586; ascending aortic distensibility, n=985) and endothelial function (flow-mediated dilation, n=777).","pmcid":"PMC7660790","score":0.6891447705030441,"pmid":32851884,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["127|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Elasticity of these large arteries changes significantly over the life span; specifically, elasticity declines with age due to arteriosclerosis (i.e., arterial hardening).","pmcid":"PMC10153623","score":0.6890075570344925,"pmid":37139101,"section":null},{"annotations":["20|8|species|9606","176|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"In general, elderly patients tend to have increased sBP and decreased dBP, caused by decreased elasticity and extensibility of large arteries occurring due to the extension of arteriosclerosis associated with increasing age.","pmcid":"PMC5492816","score":0.6884444826841355,"pmid":28685069,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["41|3|disease|MESH:D019043","200|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"In comparison to normal arterial ageing, EVA also encompasses changes in the peripheral circulation, i.e. in the smaller arterioles, therefore enhancing the cross-talk with large elastic arteries and arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC7614971","score":0.6882903176546097,"pmid":36738307,"section":null},{"annotations":["0|18|disease|MESH:C566112","157|16|disease|MESH:D001161","178|15|disease|MESH:D050197"],"text":"Arterial stiffness, carotid intima-media thickness (cIMT) and carotid elasticity, measures of arterial function and structure, are surrogates of subclinical arteriosclerosis and atherosclerosis and have been associated with cardiometabolic morbidity and mortality.","pmcid":"PMC11076203","score":0.6881737756729126,"pmid":38409590,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["157|5|species|9606","205|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Volume elastic modulus with exponential function of transmural pressure as a valid stiffness measure derived by photoplethysmographic volume-oscillometry in human finger and radial arteries: potential for arteriosclerosis screening.","pmcid":null,"score":0.6867835593223572,"pmid":34264482,"section":"title"},{"annotations":["7|3|gene|5741"],"text":"Higher PTH has been associated with impaired endothelial function, increased aortic pulse pressure, and decreased large artery elasticity.","pmcid":"PMC6190682","score":0.6863395696878434,"pmid":29400142,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["7|3|gene|5741"],"text":"Higher PTH has been associated with impaired endothelial function, increased aortic pulse pressure, and decreased large artery elasticity.","pmcid":"PMC4150218","score":0.6863395696878434,"pmid":25173540,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":null,"text":"Arterial wave reflection, endothelial function, and arterial stiffness are indicators of vascular tone modulation and large-artery elasticity, and thus, arterial function.","pmcid":"PMC9497660","score":0.6855799984931946,"pmid":36140621,"section":null},{"annotations":null,"text":"BACKGROUND: An increasing number of arterial function assessments are available, including small and large arterial elasticity (SAE/C2, LAE/C1), endothelial function as measured by flow mediated dilation (FMD), carotid intima-medial thickness (IMT), ankle brachial index (ABI), pulse pressure (PP), and pulse wave velocity (PWV).","pmcid":null,"score":0.6847731041908264,"pmid":15062880,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":null,"text":"Biologically, large artery elasticity functions well and only peripheral vascular resistance can increase diastolic blood pressure for population of this age.","pmcid":"PMC4410254","score":0.6841071432828904,"pmid":25913184,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["128|8|species|9606"],"text":"In particular, isolated systolic hypertension (systolic BP >= 140 mmHg and diastolic BP < 90 mmHg) is found in more than 80% of patients aged 80 years and older, linked to the loss of the elastic fibers in large arteries and diffuse arteriosclerosis with increase in collagen in the media and adventitia resulting in increased arterial stiffness.","pmcid":"PMC9235298","score":0.683966304063797,"pmid":35769133,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":null,"text":"Carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity, mainly reflects the elasticity of aorta, and baPWV, mainly reflects the elasticity of large and middle arteries, act as two most frequently applied indicators to evaluate arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC9366355","score":0.6837447094917297,"pmid":35966556,"section":"METHODS"},{"annotations":["15|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"The process of arteriosclerosis affects mainly the media, especially of larger vessels, and increases arterial stiffness, thereby reducing the elastic function of arteries.","pmcid":"PMC9833277","score":0.6833221447467804,"pmid":33961868,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["90|31|disease|MESH:D014188","76|8|species|9606"],"text":"We tested the hypothesis that large artery elastic function was impaired in patients with transposition of great arteries.","pmcid":null,"score":0.6831003618240357,"pmid":16618837,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["62|6|disease|None"],"text":"In a study of African American youth, found that a measure of racism-related vigilance was inversely related to large arterial elasticity (a preclinical index of cardiovascular function) for boys but not girls.","pmcid":"PMC2821669","score":0.6817137712240219,"pmid":19030981,"section":null},{"annotations":["14|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"The degree of arteriosclerosis can be assessed by measuring pulse wave velocity (PWV) between arterial sites, which reflects functional changes in large arteries.","pmcid":"PMC12482419","score":0.6814467370510101,"pmid":41023615,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":null,"text":"Effects on endothelial function and large artery elastic wall properties did not differ significantly between the two antihypertensive treatment regimens.","pmcid":null,"score":0.6806976664066314,"pmid":18194979,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["286|16|disease|MESH:D001161","184|16|disease|MESH:D016893","151|15|disease|MESH:D050197","168|6|disease|None","304|7|disease|MESH:D001159","202|29|disease|MESH:D003324","776|6|disease|MESH:D020521"],"text":"At baseline, subclinical vascular measures were collected that have been previously generalized into four uncorrelated factor composites representing: atherosclerosis (Athero: maximum carotid stenosis, coronary artery calcification, common and internal carotid intima media thickness), arteriosclerosis (Arterio: ankle brachial index, pulse pressure, distensibility coefficient, Young's Elastic Modulus, pulse wave reflection magnitude and aortic augmentation index, large and small artery elasticity, systemic vascular resistance, and total vascular impedance), blood pressure (BP: SBP, diastolic, mean arterial pressure, systolic vessel diameter on ultrasound), and cardiac function (Cardiac: pulse rate, pulse pressure amplification, estimated ejection time, and estimated stroke volume) with higher scores indicating higher burdens.","pmcid":"PMC12572826","score":0.6804491847753525,"pmid":41164889,"section":"METHODS"},{"annotations":["84|30|disease|MESH:D020765","64|3|disease|MESH:D051436","7|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Severe arteriosclerosis is a characteristic vascular feature of CKD that results in impaired large artery function.","pmcid":"PMC7929676","score":0.6782809859514236,"pmid":33680512,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["230|16|disease|MESH:D001161","19|13|chemical|MESH:D005996"],"text":"The application of nitroglycerin to relax the vascular smooth muscle of small arteries within a short time has little effect on the elastic modulus of large arteries, and the disappearance of the second wave peak is not caused by arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC10799628","score":0.6741694319248199,"pmid":38250310,"section":null},{"annotations":["138|28|disease|MESH:D017379","180|11|disease|MESH:D014693","243|16|disease|MESH:D001161","264|23|disease|MESH:D003324","10|18|disease|MESH:C566112"],"text":"Increased arterial stiffness or decreased vascular elasticity can impair arterial function, leading to increased systolic blood pressure, left ventricular hypertrophy, and reduced ventricular diastolic function, and thus increases the risk of arteriosclerosis and coronary artery disease.","pmcid":"PMC9433655","score":0.6734469187259674,"pmid":36061566,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["67|3|disease|None","280|2|disease|MESH:D002318","194|3|disease|MESH:D051436","73|24|disease|MESH:D005355","222|16|disease|MESH:D001161","170|20|disease|MESH:D002318","120|23|disease|MESH:D003324","273|3|disease|MESH:D051436","37|28|disease|MESH:D017379","17|18|disease|MESH:D004194"],"text":"Considering that myocardial disease [left ventricular hypertrophy (LVH), fibrosis and dysfunction] and not atheromatous coronary artery disease is the principal cause of CV death and disease in CKD, large elastic arteries arteriosclerosis could contribute to the effect of CKD on CV events.","pmcid":"PMC8350722","score":0.6729729813337326,"pmid":34430651,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["83|8|species|9606","97|18|disease|MESH:D024821","148|8|species|9606","162|2|disease|MESH:D007172"],"text":"In  addition, large arterial elasticity was shown to be significantly lower among  patients with metabolic syndrome compared to controls, and among patients with ED  compared to those with normal erectile function.","pmcid":"PMC11262406","score":0.6720912647247315,"pmid":39077699,"section":null},{"annotations":["137|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"PWV can reflect the elastic function of the artery as a whole, and it is widely accepted and used as the gold standard for evaluation of arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC7850680","score":0.6708113276958466,"pmid":33530239,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["229|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"In general, the elastic property of the large arteries buffers pulsation to deliver the flow with less pulsatile pressure to the peripheral microvascular; however, the coincidence of aging or cardiovascular risk factors promotes arteriosclerosis, limiting this buffering, and increases pulsatile pressure in the microvascular systems   ,  .","pmcid":"PMC8737076","score":0.6706626248359681,"pmid":33239480,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["71|5|gene|8542","300|3|gene|2489"],"text":"To our knowledge, no study to date has examined the association of the APOL1 risk variants with subclinical measures of vascular function (eg, small arterial elasticity [C2], large arterial elasticity [C1], ascending aortic distensibility [AAD]) and endothelial function (eg, flow-mediated dilation [FMD]).","pmcid":"PMC7660790","score":0.6703854668140411,"pmid":32851884,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["107|3|disease|MESH:D002318"],"text":"Similarly, our studies on arterial function, which is known to be an important marker in the assessment of CVD risk, showed no differences in commonly used indices of large artery elasticity and regulation of vascular tone, via arterial stiffness, arterial wave reflection and endothelial function testing.","pmcid":"PMC11478798","score":0.6703517991304397,"pmid":39405308,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["72|8|disease|MESH:D005355","0|16|disease|MESH:D001161","106|25|disease|MESH:D056988"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis refers to reduced arterial compliance due to increased fibrosis, loss of elasticity, and vessel wall calcification affecting the media of large and middle-sized arteries, with consecutive increase of pulse wave velocity (PWV) as measure of arterial stiffness.","pmcid":"PMC4800107","score":0.6668043553829194,"pmid":27047700,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["226|16|disease|MESH:D001161","79|4|chemical|MESH:D009569","140|15|disease|MESH:D050197"],"text":"We examined endothelial function (by flow mediated dilation, FMD, a measure of EDNO), intima-media thickness (IMT, a measure of subclinical atherosclerosis) and large artery stiffness by pulse wave velocity (PWV, a measure of arteriosclerosis).","pmcid":"PMC2860503","score":0.6630310791730881,"pmid":20436910,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["175|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"The most consistent and well-reported changes with age are luminal enlargement with wall thickening (remodeling) and stiffening at the level of large elastic arteries, namely arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC3238136","score":0.6602092093229294,"pmid":22055848,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["29|9|disease|MESH:C566112"],"text":"The main feature of arterial stiffness, specifically in the large arteries, is arteriosclerosis, which is primarily caused by structural and functional changes in the vascular media.","pmcid":"PMC10056627","score":0.6592761671543121,"pmid":36975891,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["295|16|disease|MESH:D001161","364|8|disease|MESH:D005355","377|31|disease|MESH:D002114","36|10|disease|None","76|7|gene|2006"],"text":"Previous studies showed that aortic stiffening with age is mainly caused by elastin fiber fracture, with stresses transferred to collagenous elements in an aorta which becomes progressively dilated, and also by vascular aging manifestations, displayed at the levels of large elastic arteries by arteriosclerosis originating from a gradual mechanical senescence of fibrosis and calcification of elastic fibers.","pmcid":"PMC4171684","score":0.659264771938324,"pmid":25236517,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["0|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis consists of functional depletion of large-artery elasticity.","pmcid":"PMC10496602","score":0.6563223576545716,"pmid":27355798,"section":null},{"annotations":["258|3|disease|MESH:D002318"],"text":"Our novel results extend prior evidence by showing that 9p21 is also not significantly associated with small or large artery elasticity or retinal microvascular diameters, which are functional measures of pre-clinical vascular changes predictive of clinical CVD.","pmcid":"PMC3787319","score":0.6563122338056564,"pmid":24075760,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["200|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"The most consistent and well-reported changes are luminal enlargement with wall thickening (remodeling) and reduction of elastic properties (stiffening) at the level of large elastic arteries, namely arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC3712155","score":0.655943113565445,"pmid":23864805,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["69|16|disease|MESH:D001157"],"text":"Moreover, despite ruling out large artery arteriosclerosis and small artery occlusion for current stroke etiology, the basis of cerebral vasculopathy already existed prior to stroke owing to the cardiovascular risk factor burden, which is thought to undermine the structural and functional cerebral vasculature and give rise to impaired dCA.","pmcid":"PMC7607044","score":0.6553109616041184,"pmid":33192551,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["0|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis is a degenerative process of the extracellular matrix of the arterial medial membrane, characterized by the thickening and hardening of the arterial wall due to structural and functional changes, resulting in a loss of elasticity and narrowing of the lumen.","pmcid":"PMC10521762","score":0.6515206396579742,"pmid":37767252,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["267|12|disease|MESH:D006973","203|18|disease|MESH:D012893","171|4|species|9606","342|12|disease|MESH:D006973","184|5|species|9606","400|5|species|9606"],"text":"Research reveals that race-related vigilance is positively associated with large arterial elasticity (a preclinical index of cardiovascular function) for African American boys but not girls, the risk of sleep difficulties and racial disparities in sleep, the odds of hypertension for blacks and Hispanics but not Whites and the racial gap in hypertension, and waist circumference and BMI among black women.","pmcid":"PMC6532404","score":0.6482832211256028,"pmid":30484715,"section":null},{"annotations":["127|3|disease|MESH:D002318","103|22|disease|MESH:D002318"],"text":"Functional biomarkers like large artery elasticity (LAE) and small artery elasticity (SAE) may predict cardiovascular disease (CVD) events beyond blood pressure.","pmcid":null,"score":0.6459394323825837,"pmid":21709134,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":null,"text":"Via VICORDER, indices of large artery elasticity and vascular tone regulation, including arterial stiffness, arterial-wave reflection and endothelial function can be analysed using cuff-based oscillometry.","pmcid":"PMC11478798","score":0.6442666429281235,"pmid":39405308,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["72|8|disease|MESH:D005355","0|16|disease|MESH:D001161","106|25|disease|MESH:D056988"],"text":"Arteriosclerosis refers to reduced arterial compliance due to increased fibrosis, loss of elasticity, and vessel wall calcification affecting the media of large and middle-sized arteries.","pmcid":"PMC3712155","score":0.6435163009166718,"pmid":23864805,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":null,"text":"Arteriosclerosis is a common, chronic and progressive disorder of the large elastic and muscular arteries.","pmcid":"PMC2080761","score":0.6411328172683716,"pmid":18043731,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["381|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"In response to this research question, Kotecha et al. reported that AASI is positively correlated with PP, and it is less dependent on blood pressure value and blood pressure variability than PP; it is a good supplement to PP predicting arterial elastic function, and it is recommended that AASI.PP and blood pressure variability should be used in combination in the evaluation of arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC9167089","score":0.6307099616527557,"pmid":35686157,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["129|8|disease|MESH:D009336","116|8|disease|MESH:D002545","67|7|chemical|MESH:D002118","13|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Monckeberg's arteriosclerosis may be due to the deposition of such calcium in the media of the large arteries, made ischemic and necrotic by a decrease in adventitial blood supply, as well as a decrease in luminal endothelial and intimal permeability; and also aided by chemicals derived from fragmented elastic tissue.","pmcid":null,"score":0.6235554140806199,"pmid":7273041,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["124|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Since the buffering capacity of the large arteries (i.e., the Windkessel effect) diminishes with increasing age, because of arteriosclerosis and reduction of elastic fiber, peripheral ejection of arterial blood occurs mostly during systole and is decreased during diastole, resulting in higher Skew values, being compatible with the previous results obtained for age and HR.","pmcid":"PMC7994841","score":0.6194865685701371,"pmid":33767305,"section":"DISCUSS"},{"annotations":["129|16|disease|MESH:D001161","22|15|disease|MESH:D050197"],"text":"Pathomorphologically, atherosclerosis (i.e., plaque-forming degenerative changes of the aorta and of large elastic arteries) and arteriosclerosis (i.e., concentric media thickening of muscular arteries) can be distinguished.","pmcid":null,"score":0.6168033248186111,"pmid":18815240,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":["260|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"This overlap (or lack thereof) is largely due to the speed of propagation of the pulse wave between the measurement point and the point of peripheral resistance, which, in turn, is determined by the rigidity (or lack of elasticity, i.e., arterial stiffness or arteriosclerosis) of the arterial wall (Oliver & Webb,): The greater the rigidity, the greater the pulse-wave velocity, and the greater the temporal overlap between the forward and backward waves, as indicated by the convexity of the pulse-wave shape (i.e.  PReFx) during the systole-diastole interval (Chiarelli et al.,; Fabiani et al.,).","pmcid":"PMC7006874","score":0.5786712121963501,"pmid":32043045,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":null,"text":"With increasing age, the walls of large elastic arteries undergo adverse structural and functional changes, leading to arteriosclerosis and arterial stiffness.","pmcid":"PMC10090316","score":1.0,"pmid":36883449,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["144|16|disease|MESH:D001161"],"text":"Arterial changes with aging include lumen enlargement, wall thickening, and a reduction in the elasticity of large arteries, a process known as arteriosclerosis.","pmcid":"PMC3995952","score":1.0,"pmid":24755938,"section":"INTRO"},{"annotations":["260|23|disease|MESH:D014652"],"text":"We specifically studied pulse pressure and vascular measures that reflect different anatomical sites and represent different functions of the arterial tree: (1) arterial stiffness by pulse pressure, (2) small and large arterial elasticity by tonometry and (3) endothelial dysfunction by flow mediated dilation.","pmcid":"PMC3242889","score":1.0,"pmid":22000727,"section":"abstract"},{"annotations":null,"text":"Acute effects of haemodialysis on endothelial function and large artery elasticity.","pmcid":null,"score":1.0,"pmid":11477171,"section":"title"},{"annotations":["59|22|disease|MESH:D003327","119|8|species|9606","133|14|disease|MESH:D016893","83|32|disease|MESH:D002539"],"text":"[Relationship between large artery elasticity function and coronary heart disease, lower extremity arterial disease in patients with carotid plaque].","pmcid":null,"score":1.0,"pmid":29263476,"section":"title"},{"annotations":["133|23|disease|MESH:D007680"],"text":"In summary, we found that increased pulse pressure and reduced small and large arterial elasticity are independently associated with kidney function decline among persons with eGFR >60ml/min/1.73m2.","pmcid":"PMC3242889","score":1.0,"pmid":22000727,"section":"DISCUSS"}]